						<r3d:remarks>IMOS and the repositories of the Commonwealth agencies  form the core of the AODN. Increasingly, though, universities and State government offices are offering up data resources to the AODN, and delivery of data to the AODN is being written into significant research programs e.g. National Environmental Science Program (NESP) Marine Biodiversity Hub and the Great Australian Bight research program. 
The Portal User Guide (https://help.aodn.org.au/contributing-data/) describes how to contribute to the Portal.
AODN is a regular member of the WDS.</r3d:remarks>
